An object $A$ of mass $4.0\text{ kg}$ travels at a velocity of $6.0\text{ m s}^{-1}$ to the right on a horizontal frictionless surface. It moves towards a second object $B$ of mass $2.0\text{ kg}$ that is moving at a velocity of $3.0\text{ m s}^{-1}$ in the same direction as $A$, as shown in Fig. 4.1.

{{figure:figure_4_1}}

Object $A$ collides with object $B$. The two objects join and move off together with velocity $v$.

